# Local toolchains downloaded by tools/acquire-android-toolchain.sh (android-sdk, jdk21, node22,
# mediamtx) — gigabytes of third-party binaries. The directory is ignored by contents rather than
# by name so the few real source files in it can be re-included below.
tools/*
# The acquisition scripts themselves ARE source, and are the only reason the rest of tools/ can be
# thrown away. `tools/acquire-android-toolchain.sh` had never been committed at all, which made
# BLOCKERS.md B-005a tell the reader to run a command that does not exist in a fresh clone.
!tools/*.sh
!tools/*.mjs
scrollcraft/builds/*/lab/
scrollcraft/builds/*/out/
.claude/
__pycache__/

# Working files that are not part of the product
first time review.txt
apps/web/docs/
docs/qa/local-review/

first time review 2.txt

# The phone bundle is the web build, staged by apps/mobile/scripts/stage-web.mjs.
apps/mobile/www/

# Working notes extracted from workflow results, not part of the product.
.scratch/

# Visual-inspection screenshots written by apps/web/scripts/look.mjs.
lab/

# The bundled FFmpeg binaries. They are third-party GPL builds of ~220 MB each, put in place
# reproducibly by `node tools/acquire-ffmpeg.mjs`, so they are a build input rather than source.
# What IS committed is the evidence of which build shipped: resources/ffmpeg/BUILD_INFO.txt and
# the licence texts the GPL requires to travel with the binary.
apps/desktop/resources/ffmpeg/win/*.exe
apps/desktop/resources/ffmpeg/mac/ffmpeg
apps/desktop/resources/ffmpeg/mac/ffprobe
apps/desktop/resources/ffmpeg/linux/ffmpeg
apps/desktop/resources/ffmpeg/linux/ffprobe
